<p>Or to keep people from telling his story again.</p>
<p>I didn't realize that the death lizard resembled 682 until after I wrote it, but decided to keep it in as a little easter egg. <span style="text-decoration: line-through;">But no, this&#8230; thing isn't 682. It digs all the fear that 682 creates (<em>what if there's a dimension of its species!</em>), but that's where the relation ends.</span> HEADCANON!</p>
<p>e: There's another reference hidden in one of the names. I'm curious if anyone will get it.<br />
ee: Well, there's two name references. One for funsies, the other highly relevant to our friend's identity.</p>

